                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf42902a-4c2c-3e6a-8f4d-a18ad6196350",
                                        "entry_id": "5f712f8c-85d8-3233-9652-fee9cbebbdbb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Bad or wrong administration."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f744693-db0d-4052-b8b5-2d6a5d0e86a4",
                                                "sense_id": "cf42902a-4c2c-3e6a-8f4d-a18ad6196350",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: mismanagement, misgovernance"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fa657e72-c747-4cab-b7c0-5dd41e25fe0a",
                        "source_entry_id": "2225a983-db78-3e82-a44b-d0f75795721a",
                        "source_sense_id": "de55234e-631f-31a3-a886-d51fd74a1c08",
                        "target_lang_word": "maladministration",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "maladministration",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6bca6d4d-c711-38e4-bc31-38bf45bee2eb",
                                        "entry_id": "06f1090b-6d39-338d-bca8-cce54881b59b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Faulty, improper, or inefficient administration or management, especially by a government body; (countable) an instance of this."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "affb65a7-2b2e-4da4-96e6-cfa201c5c473",
                                                "sense_id": "6bca6d4d-c711-38e4-bc31-38bf45bee2eb",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: mismanagement, misgovernance"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8417bb27-10bc-43cc-ab2b-1209e03a1d29",
                                                "sense_id": "6bca6d4d-c711-38e4-bc31-38bf45bee2eb",
                                                "text": "To combat maladministration and improve government efficiency, the ombudsman was established to function as an independent watchdog."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83a3ea78-fdd3-49e8-b60f-14d7c73ef723",
                                                "sense_id": "6bca6d4d-c711-38e4-bc31-38bf45bee2eb",
                                                "text": "At noon home to dinner, and much good discourse with him [Roger Pepys], he being mighty sensible of our misery and mal-administration. Talking of these straits we are in, he tells me that my Lord Arlington [Henry Bennet, 1st Earl of Arlington] did the last week take up £12,000 in gold, which is very likely, for all was taken up that could be."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a594750-6670-41a0-8604-403ecee3a0c9",
                                                "sense_id": "6bca6d4d-c711-38e4-bc31-38bf45bee2eb",
                                                "text": "Mean vvhile, he reſumed his taſk; and having finiſhed a moſt ſevere remonſtrance against Sir Steady, not only vvith regard to his private ingratitude, but also to his male-adminiſtration of public affairs, he ſent it to the author of a vveekly paper, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbf41720-b0dd-4f2f-a24a-01b982b57a60",
                                                "sense_id": "6bca6d4d-c711-38e4-bc31-38bf45bee2eb",
                                                "text": "[A] vvrit of error lies from hence [the court of justice-seat] to the court of king's bench, to rectify and redreſs any mal-adminiſtrations of juſtice; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bff838e8-7540-476e-9a3a-adf0cee438b7",
                                                "sense_id": "6bca6d4d-c711-38e4-bc31-38bf45bee2eb",
                                                "text": "[W]hat I wanted to get at was this fact, that the liquor traffic was, through the maladministration of the Government, opened up in a community that expected to be kept free from it. The safeguards of a prohibitory law were broken down, and the resulting debauchery took place."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11f95977-4dd0-44c8-ade9-43b180443288",
                                                "sense_id": "6bca6d4d-c711-38e4-bc31-38bf45bee2eb",
                                                "text": "Annual auditing was a farce, and since the Chambre de Justice had fallen into disuse after 1716, judicial checks on financial maladministration were non-existent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ef1ec2ec-0cc3-3c48-b2c0-f33efa17ee70",
                                        "entry_id": "06f1090b-6d39-338d-bca8-cce54881b59b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of incorrectly administering a religious rite; also, a religious group that permits such a practice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5b32fcf-60aa-48bd-bfd3-d7e3d46a5256",
                                                "sense_id": "ef1ec2ec-0cc3-3c48-b2c0-f33efa17ee70",
                                                "text": "[…] I vvould have the Sacraments on their vvheels, and yet ſo that their mal-adminiſtration bring not epidemick judgements upon us, as the receiving unvvorthily did on the Church of Corinth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7b99a036-e823-4e75-ac83-be8dc555c7d3",
                        "source_entry_id": "2225a983-db78-3e82-a44b-d0f75795721a",
                        "source_sense_id": "de55234e-631f-31a3-a886-d51fd74a1c08",
                        "target_lang_word": "mismanagement",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mismanagement",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28b051fd-e169-3ff9-8fa9-39995b7a5820",
                                        "entry_id": "d21ed638-3e0d-3942-b125-7abe027479b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The process or practice of managing ineptly, incompetently, or dishonestly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ed5a032-fb46-4992-bb7e-44841e60f1b4",
                                                "sense_id": "28b051fd-e169-3ff9-8fa9-39995b7a5820",
                                                "text": "The value of the firm's stock fell precipitously when word leaked out that officers of the company were under investigation for gross mismanagement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bdb8660-e937-4f5e-9030-8edde5e9cc13",
                                                "sense_id": "28b051fd-e169-3ff9-8fa9-39995b7a5820",
                                                "text": "But, alas! for the mismanagement of fate—he was quite out of his place in the Cortez of Spain: he dilated on religious toleration to those in whose ears it sounded like blasphemy—on the blessing of knowledge, to those with whom intellect and anarchy were synonymous—and on the rights of the people, to Hidalgos, who were preux chevaliers in loyalty to their king."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0f876f7-cd1e-4695-b470-631aea1408e4",
                                                "sense_id": "28b051fd-e169-3ff9-8fa9-39995b7a5820",
                                                "text": "[...] it also charged the Newmarket Railway £600 a year for the management or rather—as the Chairman of the Newmarket Railway did not scruple to call it—the mismanagement of the line."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c235bea-8e45-4460-ac6f-714c8fa14815",
                                                "sense_id": "28b051fd-e169-3ff9-8fa9-39995b7a5820",
                                                "text": "After decades of the type of mismanagement that proliferated across all the nationalised industries, the government was already aware that British Railways was in deep trouble."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
